1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:02,110
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:03,480
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,540 --> 00:00:05,340
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,310 --> 00:00:08,410
(Episode 13)

5
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:17,560
What brings you here?

6
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:20,560
I'm here for my portfolio.

7
00:00:21,390 --> 00:00:24,100
Oh, dear. Don't you know
submissions aren't returned?

8
00:00:24,930 --> 00:00:26,460
I'd still like it back.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,470
It's just trash to you anyway.

10
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,340
True. Wait a second.

11
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:46,080
Shouldn't you say thank you
before taking it?

12
00:00:48,250 --> 00:00:50,560
I know it was you
who ruined my score.

13
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:52,290
Says who?

14
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:53,960
Am I wrong?

15
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:56,330
That's right.
I made sure you failed.

16
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:58,560
I told you.

17
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,200
As long as I'm around,

18
00:01:00,430 --> 00:01:02,630
you'll never get a job here.

19
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:06,910
We'll see about that.

20
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:08,610
What?

21
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:12,680
You think the likes of you
can stop me?

22
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:15,310
What? The likes of me?

23
00:01:16,210 --> 00:01:17,220
You little...

24
00:01:17,720 --> 00:01:20,990
Look at you. Some habits die hard.

25
00:01:20,990 --> 00:01:22,050
Let go of me!

26
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:23,590
Hey.

27
00:01:23,820 --> 00:01:24,990
Listen up.

28
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:28,160
If I were going to quit now,
I wouldn't have even started.

29
00:01:30,430 --> 00:01:32,100
So what else can you do?

30
00:01:32,930 --> 00:01:34,300
You'll just have to wait and see.

31
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,770
So just you wait.

32
00:01:42,710 --> 00:01:44,310
I'll show you exactly what I can do.

33
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:48,480
I get it.
Of course you're feeling desperate.

34
00:01:49,450 --> 00:01:50,450
I understand.

35
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,320
You tried so hard,
only to fail because of me.

36
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:54,650
Of course you'd be upset.

37
00:01:56,520 --> 00:01:58,090
Go ahead and do whatever you want.

38
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:02,090
At this point, I'm actually curious
to see what you'll do.

39
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:06,300
What are you still doing here?

40
00:02:06,930 --> 00:02:07,970
Just get lost already.

41
00:02:09,070 --> 00:02:11,340
Fine. See you around.

42
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,640
So proud, right to the end.

43
00:02:24,180 --> 00:02:25,680
What are you going to do now?

44
00:02:26,890 --> 00:02:28,720
I have to expose
what Kang Hae Ra did.

45
00:02:29,590 --> 00:02:31,260
Expose her? To whom?

46
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,320
To the CEO.

47
00:02:34,760 --> 00:02:38,200
You know that Ms. Kang is
the CEO's daughter, right?

48
00:02:39,030 --> 00:02:40,030
Yes.

49
00:02:41,070 --> 00:02:42,700
Blood is thicker than water.

50
00:02:43,070 --> 00:02:45,500
Do you think telling the CEO
will have any effect?

51
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,410
I've got to give it a shot.

52
00:02:49,270 --> 00:02:52,440
That being said, can you find out
the CEO's schedule for me?

53
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:55,610
Sure.

54
00:03:04,090 --> 00:03:05,720
He has a meeting
with business leaders at 6 p.m.,

55
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:07,960
so he'll be leaving the office
around five.

56
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:18,870
- CEO Kang.
- What's this about?

57
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:20,640
I have something to say to the CEO.

58
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:24,910
Sir, this competition wasn't fair.

59
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:27,880
Kang Hae Ra disqualified me
out of a personal grudge.

60
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:32,420
You know my Hae Ra?

61
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:35,620
Yes, we went
to high school together.

62
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:36,960
What's your name?

63
00:03:37,690 --> 00:03:38,690
It's Ko Eun Seol.

64
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:43,530
So you're saying my Hae Ra
deliberately disqualified you?

65
00:03:44,230 --> 00:03:45,230
Yes.

66
00:03:45,930 --> 00:03:48,700
I'd like you to review
my portfolio again.

67
00:03:49,930 --> 00:03:52,500
If that's what this is about,
talk to the staff in charge.

68
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,240
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir. Move aside.

69
00:04:19,700 --> 00:04:22,130
What are you looking at
so seriously?

70
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:25,140
Unbelievable.

71
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,270
When will Hae Ra be home?

72
00:04:27,910 --> 00:04:29,040
She should be here soon.

73
00:04:30,110 --> 00:04:32,480
It's the judge's score sheet
for the competition.

74
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,120
What is it? Is there a problem?

75
00:04:37,450 --> 00:04:39,020
I'm home.

76
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,090
Hae Ra, come here.

77
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:42,950
Why?

78
00:04:43,790 --> 00:04:46,420
Is contestant number 97 Ko Eun Seol?

79
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:49,090
How do you know that, Dad?

80
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,700
And she was your classmate?

81
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:52,800
Don't tell me she came to see you.

82
00:04:53,260 --> 00:04:54,270
She did.

83
00:04:54,370 --> 00:04:56,800
She said you disqualified her
for personal reasons.

84
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:58,400
Unbelievable.

85
00:04:59,200 --> 00:05:01,710
Can you do anything right?

86
00:05:02,310 --> 00:05:05,180
Dad, I was just making sure
the guidelines were followed.

87
00:05:05,210 --> 00:05:07,080
She's the one who broke them.

88
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:09,710
Then why did all the other judges
give her high scores?

89
00:05:11,650 --> 00:05:12,720
Well, that's...

90
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:14,850
If you wanted to fail her,

91
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,490
you shouldn't have made it
so obvious.

92
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:19,520
What will you do if she goes
to the press and says...

93
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:21,060
the CEO's daughter
is power-tripping?

94
00:05:21,790 --> 00:05:24,100
Surely she wouldn't go that far.

95
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,100
That's because you haven't met her.

96
00:05:27,370 --> 00:05:28,930
She's no pushover.

97
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:32,200
Then just reverse the decision now.

98
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:34,640
You said all the other judges
gave her high scores.

99
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:36,510
Absolutely not, Mom.

100
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:39,010
Yes, Hae Ra is right about that.

101
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:40,410
If we reverse the decision now,

102
00:05:40,910 --> 00:05:42,810
it'd be like admitting the company
made a mistake.

103
00:05:43,880 --> 00:05:46,850
Then what? What if she goes around
telling everyone, like you said?

104
00:05:48,050 --> 00:05:49,290
I don't think she'll do that.

105
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:53,090
How can you be so sure,
Director Joo?

106
00:05:54,530 --> 00:05:57,230
If anything like that happens,
I'll handle it myself.

107
00:05:57,460 --> 00:05:59,060
Please don't worry too much, sir.

108
00:06:00,300 --> 00:06:02,170
Anyway, Hae Ra,

109
00:06:03,030 --> 00:06:05,870
keep disappointing me
and see what happens.

110
00:06:09,610 --> 00:06:10,610
Ko Eun Seol...

111
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:13,340
So the best you could do
was tattle to my dad?

112
00:06:15,410 --> 00:06:16,410
Hae Ra.

113
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,220
Did you really disqualify
your friend on purpose?

114
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:22,650
A friend, as if.
She's my worst enemy.

115
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:28,830
She's so immature.
What am I going to do with her?

116
00:06:35,430 --> 00:06:36,430
How did it go?

117
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:37,940
Were you able to meet with the CEO?

118
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:41,710
Yes.
But you were right, Attorney Seo.

119
00:06:42,170 --> 00:06:43,710
He wouldn't even give me
the time of day.

120
00:06:45,110 --> 00:06:46,240
I figured as much.

121
00:06:47,910 --> 00:06:49,810
That must've really upset you.

122
00:06:50,380 --> 00:06:53,650
Well, I was somewhat prepared
for it, so I'm fine.

123
00:06:54,990 --> 00:06:57,220
You don't have to act tough with me.

124
00:06:59,990 --> 00:07:01,060
Anyway,

125
00:07:01,430 --> 00:07:03,090
now that even the CEO
has turned you down,

126
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,160
what's your next move?

127
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,830
If the CEO won't help,
I'll have to go see Chairman Kim.

128
00:07:08,670 --> 00:07:10,870
Do you really think
she won't favor her own side?

129
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,740
I have to hope
that she'll be different.

130
00:07:23,750 --> 00:07:26,820
I'd like you to review
my portfolio again.

131
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:30,450
If that's what this is about,
talk to the staff in charge.

132
00:07:30,890 --> 00:07:32,960
- Let's go.
- Yes, sir. Move aside.

133
00:07:44,900 --> 00:07:46,000
Mr. Seok Jin.

134
00:07:47,710 --> 00:07:49,670
- Mr. Seok Jin.
- Yes?

135
00:07:49,970 --> 00:07:50,980
What is it, Mom?

136
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:53,340
I asked
what you thought of my drawing.

137
00:07:54,210 --> 00:07:55,210
Right.

138
00:07:56,450 --> 00:07:58,220
No way. It's really good.

139
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:00,850
You're getting better and better.

140
00:08:03,720 --> 00:08:04,790
But...

141
00:08:05,390 --> 00:08:07,630
Mr. Seok Jin, you seem upset.

142
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:09,960
Oh, right.

143
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:12,230
It's not what you think.

144
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,530
There's just someone
I can't stop thinking about.

145
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:16,630
Who is it?

146
00:08:19,570 --> 00:08:21,940
Just someone. Someone who hurt me.

147
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:24,740
How mean of them.

148
00:08:26,110 --> 00:08:27,480
Should I teach them a lesson?

149
00:08:31,350 --> 00:08:33,250
Anyway, this stands for love.

150
00:08:34,890 --> 00:08:38,960
That Ko Eun Seol girl might
come to see you as well,

151
00:08:38,990 --> 00:08:40,660
so I'll escort you myself
for a while.

152
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,060
Is that really necessary?

153
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:46,460
If she shows up,
I can just calm her down.

154
00:08:46,530 --> 00:08:47,900
Absolutely not.

155
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:55,010
If you give her an inch,
she'll take a mile.

156
00:08:55,070 --> 00:08:56,840
You have to nip it in the bud.

157
00:08:58,710 --> 00:08:59,810
All right.

158
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:09,850
What's this?

159
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,860
- You're as beautiful as ever,
- My gosh.

160
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:13,490
actress Kim Jung Sun.

161
00:09:17,090 --> 00:09:18,530
What is it, ma'am?

162
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,570
I think it's him.

163
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:23,570
The stalker.

164
00:09:27,910 --> 00:09:29,710
Didn't you say he was in prison?

165
00:09:31,380 --> 00:09:32,880
He must've been released.

166
00:09:33,710 --> 00:09:35,710
Then what do I do?

167
00:09:37,650 --> 00:09:38,720
Don't worry.

168
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:40,350
I'll assign you a security detail.

169
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:50,860
(Cheongchun Gositel)

170
00:09:55,630 --> 00:09:57,070
It was originally mine.

171
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:01,240
I'm just taking it back.

172
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,040
I...

173
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:07,310
I have to get into Cheongma,
no matter what.

174
00:10:28,070 --> 00:10:29,370
What's this?

175
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,840
- Did he leave this here?
- Get rid of it now.

176
00:10:37,440 --> 00:10:40,310
Madam Chairman. Ma'am!

177
00:10:40,310 --> 00:10:41,780
- You can't do this here.
- Please.

178
00:10:41,780 --> 00:10:43,080
It'll only take a moment.

179
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:44,380
- Leave.
- Ma'am!

180
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:47,920
- Please. Just let me talk to her.
- You can't.

181
00:10:48,050 --> 00:10:51,720
Ma'am, just a moment. Ma'am!

182
00:10:51,790 --> 00:10:54,760
Ma'am, please hear me out.
Madam Chairman!

183
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,580
Here, have some of this.

184
00:11:13,910 --> 00:11:14,950
Thanks.

185
00:11:15,110 --> 00:11:17,820
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

186
00:11:19,780 --> 00:11:21,150
Are you feeling better now?

187
00:11:23,150 --> 00:11:24,160
Yes.

188
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:28,030
Mom. I heard your stalker showed up.

189
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:31,930
- He did.
- He left flowers at the house.

190
00:11:32,060 --> 00:11:33,300
That's insane.

191
00:11:34,070 --> 00:11:35,830
So, are you okay?

192
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:38,870
Yes, I'm fine.

193
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:43,270
What should we do about
next week's 50th anniversary event?

194
00:11:43,740 --> 00:11:46,680
Perhaps we should cancel
your appearance on the runway.

195
00:11:47,010 --> 00:11:48,380
Of course.

196
00:11:48,410 --> 00:11:51,350
I'll take your place,
so don't worry, Mom.

197
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:55,790
No. If I cancel, that means he wins,

198
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:57,190
and I can't let that happen.

199
00:11:58,390 --> 00:11:59,420
But still...

200
00:11:59,690 --> 00:12:01,290
Won't it be too dangerous?

201
00:12:01,990 --> 00:12:04,160
Director Joo will be there,
and so will the bodyguards.

202
00:12:04,230 --> 00:12:05,600
What's there to worry about?

203
00:12:08,530 --> 00:12:09,530
By the way,

204
00:12:10,430 --> 00:12:12,270
that young woman from earlier...

205
00:12:12,340 --> 00:12:13,840
She must be Hae Ra's old classmate.

206
00:12:14,570 --> 00:12:16,040
I guess so.

207
00:12:16,440 --> 00:12:18,680
Wait, did Ko Eun Seol
come to see you too?

208
00:12:19,910 --> 00:12:21,980
She's even crazier than I thought.

209
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,720
She's the young woman from before.

210
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:28,820
From before?
Who are you talking about?

211
00:12:29,290 --> 00:12:33,760
The girl who saved her dad
as "My Dearest Dad" in her contacts.

212
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:35,060
No way.

213
00:12:35,290 --> 00:12:37,290
Are you saying you compared me
to a girl like that?

214
00:12:39,100 --> 00:12:41,700
Hae Ra, why do you hate her so much?

215
00:12:41,770 --> 00:12:43,230
She seemed nice enough.

216
00:12:43,300 --> 00:12:45,100
What's so nice about her?

217
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,340
Mom, are you seriously praising her
in front of me?

218
00:12:47,470 --> 00:12:48,510
Team Leader Kang!

219
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:51,280
The Chairman is in shock
and having a hard time.

220
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:53,640
What are you doing? That's enough.

221
00:12:56,010 --> 00:12:57,010
Fine.

222
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:01,750
Ma'am, you shouldn't worry
about a girl like that anymore.

223
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:03,820
I guess...

224
00:13:03,920 --> 00:13:05,690
I have my own problems.

225
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:12,030
Here, have some water.

226
00:13:19,070 --> 00:13:20,200
What are you doing here?

227
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:23,640
I'm here to see Chairman Kim.

228
00:13:25,610 --> 00:13:28,250
Have you been waiting here
like this all day?

229
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:30,280
Yes.

230
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,050
Let's go talk somewhere.

231
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:36,750
We can talk here.

232
00:13:36,750 --> 00:13:37,820
Follow me.

233
00:13:49,830 --> 00:13:51,200
Do you really have to go this far?

234
00:13:51,870 --> 00:13:53,500
- What do you mean?
- You're doing this...

235
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:55,010
because you think you got wronged.

236
00:13:55,210 --> 00:13:57,070
- That's right.
- Exactly.

237
00:13:57,840 --> 00:13:59,540
So, is this really necessary?

238
00:14:00,410 --> 00:14:02,910
Like you said,
I was unfairly eliminated.

239
00:14:05,380 --> 00:14:07,080
This won't change anything.

240
00:14:07,550 --> 00:14:09,190
You'll only end up
looking more pathetic.

241
00:14:10,420 --> 00:14:11,820
So just stop here.

242
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:17,460
Is that what you wanted
to talk to me about?

243
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,160
Ko Eun Seol...

244
00:14:19,430 --> 00:14:21,300
Since you're involved,
you must know...

245
00:14:21,370 --> 00:14:22,730
that Kang Hae Ra gave me a zero.

246
00:14:22,830 --> 00:14:26,900
She was just exercising
her authority as a judge.

247
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:29,540
It was an abuse of power
under the guise of authority.

248
00:14:32,810 --> 00:14:34,710
Why are you going to such lengths?

249
00:14:35,110 --> 00:14:37,450
Are you this desperate
to get into Cheongma?

250
00:14:38,680 --> 00:14:39,750
Yes.

251
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:41,050
What?

252
00:14:41,950 --> 00:14:43,790
If we're done here,
I'll be on my way.

253
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:02,470
Please, have a seat.

254
00:15:05,580 --> 00:15:08,650
Ms. Joo,
what brings you to my office?

255
00:15:09,580 --> 00:15:11,980
Chairman Kim's stalker
was released from prison.

256
00:15:13,950 --> 00:15:16,020
The man who was arrested
two years ago?

257
00:15:16,850 --> 00:15:17,860
Yes.

258
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:20,420
Has he made contact again since?

259
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:23,260
Here.

260
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,330
(You're as beautiful as ever,
actress Kim Jung Sun.)

261
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:34,340
Is this enough to get
a restraining order?

262
00:15:35,370 --> 00:15:36,570
It's certainly worth a try.

263
00:15:37,510 --> 00:15:40,710
Will it be possible
before next week's 50th anniversary event?

264
00:15:42,180 --> 00:15:43,780
I can't guarantee that.

265
00:15:44,050 --> 00:15:45,520
There's a procedure
we have to follow.

266
00:15:47,020 --> 00:15:48,020
Then,

267
00:15:48,090 --> 00:15:50,550
it seems we have no choice
but to increase security.

268
00:15:53,090 --> 00:15:54,090
Right.

269
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:03,830
Yes, this is it.
You can stop here, please.

270
00:16:03,900 --> 00:16:05,870
Okay, get as close as you can.

271
00:16:05,940 --> 00:16:07,470
Yes, that's good.

272
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:10,010
Eun Guk, come on, let's go.

273
00:16:15,910 --> 00:16:17,110
Welcome.

274
00:16:17,450 --> 00:16:18,920
Right, hello.

275
00:17:08,670 --> 00:17:11,440
Thanks again
for letting us rent the annex.

276
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,470
Well, it's not like
I'm letting you stay for free.

277
00:17:16,470 --> 00:17:17,980
I know, but still.

278
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:22,580
But you should really do something
about your son's clothes.

279
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:24,750
Come on, it's embarrassing.

280
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:26,650
What's wrong with my clothes?

281
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:31,820
Should I wear long sleeves
when it's boiling hot?

282
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,730
My gosh, that's gross.

283
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:37,530
So many people would kill
for this body.

284
00:17:37,930 --> 00:17:39,160
She doesn't get it.

285
00:17:46,070 --> 00:17:48,510
You shameless punk.

286
00:17:56,680 --> 00:17:58,950
- Okay, I think we're almost done.
- Right.

287
00:17:58,950 --> 00:18:00,250
Should we order jjajangmyeon?

288
00:18:00,320 --> 00:18:04,150
Oh, good idea.
But first, go get your grandma.

289
00:18:04,890 --> 00:18:06,220
Oh, right. Grandma.

290
00:18:07,190 --> 00:18:08,890
Got it. I'll go get her now.

291
00:18:08,890 --> 00:18:11,330
- Okay. And be nice about it.
- Sure.

292
00:18:11,330 --> 00:18:15,400
If she won't budge,
try tempting her with jjajangmyeon.

293
00:18:26,180 --> 00:18:28,950
Don't tell me
they actually ditched me.

294
00:18:28,950 --> 00:18:29,950
Grandma.

295
00:18:33,650 --> 00:18:34,720
Grandma,

296
00:18:35,150 --> 00:18:38,020
we're done with the move,
so let's go.

297
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,490
How many times do I have to tell you
I'm not going?

298
00:18:40,490 --> 00:18:42,590
Don't be like that. Let's go.

299
00:18:43,630 --> 00:18:46,360
Then, don't let Eun Seol
into the house.

300
00:18:46,800 --> 00:18:48,330
I can't do that, Grandma.

301
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:50,670
Eun Guk, you...

302
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:54,070
If you hate Eun Seol that much,

303
00:18:54,370 --> 00:18:56,810
then you should go ask
your favorite fortune-teller.

304
00:18:56,970 --> 00:18:58,940
Ask them
whether Eun Seol really did it.

305
00:18:59,010 --> 00:19:01,350
I already did.
You think I wouldn't have?

306
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,280
And?

307
00:19:03,810 --> 00:19:05,220
What did they say?

308
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,650
They said Eun Seol
didn't do it, right?

309
00:19:10,090 --> 00:19:12,590
But you can't believe everything
a fortune-teller says.

310
00:19:13,220 --> 00:19:15,630
At this point,
it's not that you can't believe it.

311
00:19:15,690 --> 00:19:17,030
It's that you don't want
to believe it.

312
00:19:17,330 --> 00:19:19,930
You're actually hoping that
Eun Seol really did it.

313
00:19:20,060 --> 00:19:23,300
What? What kind of person
do you take me for?

314
00:19:23,470 --> 00:19:25,840
No matter
how much I may hate Eun Seol,

315
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:27,270
how could you say
something like that?

316
00:19:28,010 --> 00:19:30,570
Then if you don't want me
to think that,

317
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:31,780
get up right now.

318
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,580
Because if you don't,

319
00:19:34,710 --> 00:19:36,380
I'm just going to keep
thinking that.

320
00:19:36,780 --> 00:19:38,180
But...

321
00:19:39,350 --> 00:19:40,350
See?

322
00:19:40,550 --> 00:19:42,450
It feels unfair to be misunderstood,
doesn't it?

323
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:46,060
Imagine how Eun Seol must feel.

324
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,630
Grandma, you're hungry, aren't you?

325
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:54,000
Gosh, I'm starving too.

326
00:19:54,830 --> 00:19:56,100
So let's go quickly...

327
00:19:56,170 --> 00:19:58,800
and order jjajangmyeon,
your favorite. Okay?

328
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:02,370
- Come on.
- Just stop it.

329
00:20:02,440 --> 00:20:04,740
My bag. Okay, I'll get up.

330
00:20:06,410 --> 00:20:07,410
Let's go.

331
00:20:13,020 --> 00:20:14,690
Oh, hey. Welcome home.

332
00:20:15,790 --> 00:20:18,220
I'm sorry I couldn't help
with the move, Dad.

333
00:20:18,290 --> 00:20:19,720
It wasn't much of a move.

334
00:20:19,790 --> 00:20:21,330
We pretty much
threw everything away.

335
00:20:27,760 --> 00:20:28,770
You're here.

336
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:30,570
It's been a while, Eun Guk.

337
00:20:32,870 --> 00:20:34,870
Grandma, Eun Seol's here.

338
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:40,540
So what if she's here?
What do you want me to do?

339
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:41,880
Mom, come on.

340
00:20:42,610 --> 00:20:44,950
Go on in and get some rest.
You must be tired.

341
00:20:45,780 --> 00:20:47,480
- Okay.
- Right.

342
00:20:49,250 --> 00:20:50,820
- Unbelievable.
- Unbelievable.

343
00:20:51,050 --> 00:20:53,390
You should go rest too, Mom.
You must be tired.

344
00:20:53,390 --> 00:20:54,860
You go rest.

345
00:20:58,630 --> 00:21:01,500
Why go through all the hassle
of getting a restraining order?

346
00:21:01,770 --> 00:21:05,370
Just have him thrown in jail,
or hire someone to scare him off.

347
00:21:05,370 --> 00:21:07,270
Do you think
this is a lawless country?

348
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:08,940
We can't just throw people in jail.

349
00:21:09,010 --> 00:21:11,070
He's not just anyone.
He's a stalker.

350
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:13,140
Besides, there are laws.

351
00:21:13,340 --> 00:21:15,610
Should the owner's family
act above them?

352
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:18,380
Are you trying to ruin the company?

353
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:20,220
Honestly,

354
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:22,420
how does it make sense
that the Chairman of Cheongma...

355
00:21:22,420 --> 00:21:23,550
is being threatened by a stalker?

356
00:21:23,650 --> 00:21:25,060
We have money and connections.

357
00:21:25,160 --> 00:21:27,460
It's ridiculous
we can't handle one stalker.

358
00:21:27,520 --> 00:21:29,090
The CEO is right.

359
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:32,660
If things go wrong, the perpetrator
could be seen as the victim.

360
00:21:32,960 --> 00:21:35,370
That would be a huge risk
for the company.

361
00:21:35,800 --> 00:21:37,470
It's best to do things legally.

362
00:21:37,530 --> 00:21:40,140
I've seen plenty of people
get burned for trusting the law.

363
00:21:40,640 --> 00:21:43,610
What's the point of having
all this money and power?

364
00:21:43,610 --> 00:21:44,910
This is so frustrating.

365
00:21:47,010 --> 00:21:48,150
- Unbelievable.
- My gosh.

366
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:53,350
You don't need to worry
about him either.

367
00:21:53,780 --> 00:21:55,250
We have bodyguards.

368
00:21:56,150 --> 00:21:57,950
You don't know
unless you've lived it.

369
00:21:58,220 --> 00:21:59,820
The pain is so real.

370
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:21,340
What are you doing out here?

371
00:22:22,350 --> 00:22:23,480
Attorney Seo.

372
00:22:24,550 --> 00:22:25,750
I couldn't sleep.

373
00:22:29,090 --> 00:22:30,090
By the way,

374
00:22:30,550 --> 00:22:33,620
is there really no way
I can meet Chairman Kim?

375
00:22:39,260 --> 00:22:42,600
Well, there's next week's
50th anniversary event.

376
00:22:43,970 --> 00:22:45,540
The 50th anniversary event?

377
00:22:47,070 --> 00:22:50,040
Chairman Kim is scheduled
to walk the runway that day.

378
00:22:51,940 --> 00:22:54,810
So I could create an opportunity?

379
00:22:58,550 --> 00:23:00,450
Please, get me in.

380
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:03,020
I'll handle the rest from there.

381
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:07,460
All right.
I'll get you an invitation,

382
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:08,630
and you can give it a shot.

383
00:23:08,690 --> 00:23:12,030
But you have to be
extremely careful.

384
00:23:12,030 --> 00:23:13,030
Okay?

385
00:23:13,400 --> 00:23:14,400
Got it.

386
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:23,770
(Lowering Barriers,
Filling Lives With Warmth)

387
00:23:23,770 --> 00:23:27,110
(Cheongma Group
50th Anniversary Event)

388
00:23:32,620 --> 00:23:33,680
Yes, Attorney Seo.

389
00:23:33,920 --> 00:23:36,890
Chairman Kim is
in the basement waiting room.

390
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:38,320
Okay, got it.

391
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:09,490
How did you get in here?

392
00:24:15,730 --> 00:24:16,960
I was invited.

393
00:24:19,030 --> 00:24:20,100
Who invited you?

394
00:24:21,930 --> 00:24:23,070
Show me your invitation.

395
00:24:29,170 --> 00:24:30,170
Satisfied?

396
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,470
Where are you going?

397
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:00,100
I'm just going to the restroom.

398
00:25:17,050 --> 00:25:19,060
- Madam Chairman!
- Be quiet.

399
00:25:20,090 --> 00:25:21,420
Or this woman dies.

400
00:25:22,660 --> 00:25:23,660
All right.

401
00:25:24,430 --> 00:25:27,030
Okay, I get it. Just calm down.

402
00:25:30,530 --> 00:25:32,100
What do you want from me?

403
00:25:32,800 --> 00:25:34,370
Why are you doing this?

404
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:37,940
You still don't know?

405
00:25:38,810 --> 00:25:40,580
There's only one thing I want.

406
00:25:41,310 --> 00:25:42,380
Your love.

407
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:45,820
Please, don't do this.

408
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:48,950
Let's talk this out.

409
00:25:50,020 --> 00:25:51,020
No.

410
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:53,220
I'm exhausted now.

411
00:25:54,290 --> 00:25:55,890
If I can't have you,

412
00:25:56,590 --> 00:25:57,890
we might as well die together.

413
00:25:58,230 --> 00:25:59,760
Today's that day.

414
00:25:59,960 --> 00:26:03,070
Please... Please don't do this.

415
00:26:03,430 --> 00:26:05,440
This isn't love.

416
00:26:09,370 --> 00:26:10,840
Ma'am, run!

417
00:26:30,460 --> 00:26:32,100
Help!

418
00:26:32,300 --> 00:26:34,060
- Help.
- Are you all right?

419
00:26:34,330 --> 00:26:35,430
In there...

420
00:26:41,710 --> 00:26:43,310
No, my love.

421
00:26:47,810 --> 00:26:48,810
Ma'am!

422
00:26:49,950 --> 00:26:51,210
Ma'am, are you all right?

423
00:26:51,880 --> 00:26:56,150
I'm fine. Go check inside. Hurry.

424
00:27:03,860 --> 00:27:04,860
Oh no.

425
00:27:05,860 --> 00:27:08,300
Eun Seol, are you okay?

426
00:27:10,630 --> 00:27:11,630
Blood...

427
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,200
Are you okay?

428
00:27:15,110 --> 00:27:16,110
I'm okay.

429
00:27:16,610 --> 00:27:17,610
You're bleeding.

430
00:27:24,550 --> 00:27:26,280
- Oh no.
- What happened?

431
00:28:00,320 --> 00:28:01,620
- Easy now.
- Okay.

432
00:28:13,900 --> 00:28:14,900
Thank you.

433
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,740
I can't believe this.

434
00:28:22,010 --> 00:28:23,670
Do you not have any fear at all?

435
00:28:24,140 --> 00:28:25,980
What were you thinking,
taking on someone with a knife?

436
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:28,480
It was a desperate situation.

437
00:28:28,610 --> 00:28:30,080
It doesn't matter
how desperate it was.

438
00:28:30,710 --> 00:28:31,880
Do you have a death wish?

439
00:28:33,120 --> 00:28:34,450
Why are you mad at me?

440
00:28:34,550 --> 00:28:36,750
I wasn't the one
waving a knife around.

441
00:28:39,590 --> 00:28:41,160
I'm sorry to ask,

442
00:28:41,830 --> 00:28:43,590
but could you see
if I can switch rooms?

443
00:28:44,290 --> 00:28:45,560
This is a little much.

444
00:28:47,300 --> 00:28:48,330
Don't worry about it.

445
00:28:51,230 --> 00:28:54,270
Anyway, how's Chairman Kim?

446
00:29:02,010 --> 00:29:04,580
Ma'am, are you okay?

447
00:29:06,720 --> 00:29:07,780
Where am I?

448
00:29:09,750 --> 00:29:11,650
Don't worry. You're home.

449
00:29:14,990 --> 00:29:16,030
I'm sorry.

450
00:29:16,490 --> 00:29:18,460
I should've paid closer attention.

451
00:29:19,730 --> 00:29:23,030
Who would've thought he'd be hiding
in the women's restroom?

452
00:29:25,370 --> 00:29:27,000
But what about that young woman?

453
00:29:27,540 --> 00:29:28,740
Was she badly hurt?

454
00:29:29,510 --> 00:29:34,110
No, she just needed a few stitches.
You don't need to worry.

455
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:40,520
If it hadn't been for her,
something awful could've happened.

456
00:29:41,990 --> 00:29:44,920
Try not to think about it
and get some more sleep.

457
00:29:45,360 --> 00:29:48,790
The sedative is kicking in now,
so you'll calm down soon.

458
00:29:52,530 --> 00:29:53,630
Get some sleep, okay?

459
00:30:06,610 --> 00:30:08,040
Why did it have to be Ko Eun Seol?

460
00:30:12,280 --> 00:30:13,450
How's my wife?

461
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:17,690
She was just given a sedative.
She should be fine now.

462
00:30:18,590 --> 00:30:20,290
How did the anniversary event go?

463
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:23,530
Given the scene this morning,
do you think it turned out okay?

464
00:30:24,260 --> 00:30:27,200
Why weren't you there
escorting her, Director Joo?

465
00:30:28,200 --> 00:30:30,200
I'm very sorry, sir.

466
00:32:12,040 --> 00:32:15,810
(A Trap Called Desire)

467
00:32:15,910 --> 00:32:18,570
- Kang Hae Ra.
- You don't care how I feel, do you?

468
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:20,010
Do you have any idea
how I felt earlier?

469
00:32:20,010 --> 00:32:21,410
My blood ran cold.

470
00:32:21,710 --> 00:32:23,750
I'm the one
who's disappointed in you.

471
00:32:24,050 --> 00:32:25,420
Do you two know each other?

472
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:28,850
Now that Attorney Seo is here,
you can go, Seok Jin.

473
00:32:28,990 --> 00:32:30,490
No way, Mom.

474
00:32:30,820 --> 00:32:32,990
A stranger would think Ko Eun Seol
is your daughter, not me.

475
00:32:33,420 --> 00:32:35,330
How can I be another burden to you?

476
00:32:35,530 --> 00:32:37,390
No matter how I think about it,
it's just not right.

477
00:32:37,630 --> 00:32:40,500
I'd like to offer you
financial compensation.

478
00:32:40,660 --> 00:32:43,030
I'd like a job at Cheongma.

479
00:32:43,330 --> 00:32:44,770
That's out of the question, Ms. Ko.

480
00:32:46,170 --> 00:32:48,170
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
